{
  "note": "The bar. Every ingredient any drink on the menu can call for. `kind` groups the shelf, `unit` tells the notation parser how to read a bare number, `staple` marks what is assumed always on hand, `shelf` overrides the name where the bottle and the pour want different words for the same thing, `notes` is a house recipe for making that bottle \u2014 the checkbox ticks the shelf, the rest of the row reveals the notes when there are any. `bottles` is the shopping list for that type, grouped by quality; ticking a brand ticks the parent, and the last brand unticked unticks it. `catalog` marks a type that is on the shopping list before any drink calls for it. Garnish is stocked like anything else \u2014 the letter lives in the serve token, and notation.json says which bottle it calls for \u2014 but it is optional, so it never decides whether a drink can be poured.",
  "bottles_copy": "When it comes to base liquor, anything above excellent is made for sipping neat. This does not mean the quality of the bottles in the solid or elevated lists is poor, quite the opposite: staples like Four Roses Bourbon and Beefeater London Dry Gin are nearly perfect representations of their categories, but that kind of makes them boring for a neat sip, yet a solid foundation for a cocktail expecting their familiar flavor profile.",
  "kinds": [
    { "id": "base",     "label": "Base spirits",  "blurb": "Ten bottles carry the whole menu." },
    { "id": "vermouth", "label": "Vermouth",      "blurb": "Two bottles. Refrigerate them." },
    { "id": "modifier", "label": "Modifiers",     "blurb": "Where the range actually comes from." },
    { "id": "bitters",  "label": "Bitters",       "blurb": "Measured in dashes." },
    { "id": "syrup",    "label": "Syrups",        "blurb": "Made at home. Weigh everything \u2014 a kitchen scale is required. Three to four weeks in the fridge, sealed." },
    { "id": "juice",    "label": "Citrus",        "blurb": "Squeezed to order. The peel is the garnish." },
    { "id": "garnish",  "label": "Garnish",       "blurb": "The tail of every code. Optional, so it is never counted against a drink." },
    { "id": "other",    "label": "Other",         "blurb": "" }
  ],
